[Effect](/lore/effect-basics) 4's [`Effect.validate`](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/effect%404.0.0/packages/effect/src/Effect.ts#L594-L651) evaluates every collection element.
It returns all failures as a non-empty array when any element fails.
Successful values are discarded in that case.

The [code-snippets design brief](/lore/code-snippets) uses this operation for preflight.
Each snippet is an independent job.
A job stops when a dependent stage fails.
Other jobs still run.

The proposed order is:
1. Collect snippet jobs.
2. Check every job.
3. Report each failure with [diagnostic context](/lore/errors-are-part-of-the-interface).
4. Write assets only when preflight succeeds.

Error accumulation means reporting every independent failure together. Here it runs across jobs. Each job must pass validation before highlighting.

The planned property inserts exactly `k` independent failures.
It expects exactly `k` diagnostics and zero asset writes.
See [property-based testing](/lore/property-based-testing) and [the glossary](/glossary).
